      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:credentials",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Recover and use authentication material\n\nStart with an artifact produced by an actual read, query, session or collection source; the artifact type and username may still be unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nRecover and use authentication material\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Identify the artifact before using a cracking tool\n\nKeep provenance and local/domain/application account scope. Hash-looking text is not automatically an NT hash.\n\n```bash\nfile FILE\nhead -c 160 FILE\n```\n\n**Classify the artifact and its identity context — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A plaintext password\n\nTest the matching identity on one relevant reachable service.\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 845,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### An SSH private key\n\nCheck key format, protection and the intended account.\n\n**Inspect and recover SSH private-key access — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-0-finding-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1070,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A ticket/cache\n\nCheck principal, service scope, expiry and a compatible client.\n\n**Classify tickets and use a compatible cache — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nFormat is still unknown: inspect the artifact before selecting a Hashcat/John mode.\n\n**Classify the artifact and its identity context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "## Use Hashcat/John only after format identification\n\nSelect the documented format-specific mode and an offline candidate list; recovery is not proof of service access.\n\n```bash\nhashcat -a 0 -m MODE hashes.txt wordlist.txt -r /usr/share/hashcat/rules/best64.rule --session job\nhashcat -m MODE hashes.txt --show\n```\n\n**Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A password is recovered\n\nValidate the account scope and relevant service permission.\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1700,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A reusable NT hash rather than a recoverable plaintext password\n\nUse only protocols and clients supporting that material.\n\n**Recover or reuse an NT password hash — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:credentials:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nNo recovery: revisit artifact type and feasible candidates; enumerate other evidence instead of assuming the account is unusable.\n\n**Classify the artifact and its identity context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:credentials",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/credentials.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:credentials",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3385,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\nA secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 3345,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nfile FILE\nhead -c 160 FILE\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3325,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nHeaders and producing context distinguish a private key, challenge response and stored NT verifier.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3571,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRecord the exact source, user/domain and complete format; identify compatible recovery/authentication operations.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3275,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nSource and format agree on the type: route it to the matching recovery/use method.\n\n**Verify:** Identify artifact type, source, account/domain and compatible next operation; record unknowns instead of guessing.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#credential-classify|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3616,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe value is an application identifier rather than an authentication artifact: reject the credential hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3837,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA bare hexadecimal string without provenance does not identify its algorithm; investigate the producing application.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3275,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nSOURCE -> MATERIAL/FORMAT -> LOCAL/DOMAIN/APPLICATION IDENTITY\n-> POSSIBLE USE -> SERVICE/PROTOCOL -> AUTHENTICATION\n-> AUTHORIZATION -> NEW ACCESS -> RE-ENUMERATION\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#credential-classify|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3641,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3948,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n**Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4255,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Classify tickets and use a compatible cache\n\n**When:** A ccache/kirbi file or an existing ticket cache\n\n**Still required:** Correct principal/realm, valid lifetime, service scope, compatible cache format and naming/KDC route\n\n**Classify tickets and use a compatible cache — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4562,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover a protected KeePass database password\n\n**When:** A readable KeePass database and possible associated key file\n\n**Still required:** Complete database, compatible converter, and every required factor; a feasible password candidate strategy\n\n**Recover a protected KeePass database password — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4869,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect and recover SSH private-key access\n\n**When:** A private key from a file read, share, repository or home directory\n\n**Still required:** Correct key format, passphrase if encrypted, matching server account/key authorization and accepted algorithm/policy\n\n**Inspect and recover SSH private-key access — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5176,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover Linux account passwords from matched records\n\n**When:** Readable password verifiers and account metadata\n\n**Still required:** Correct passwd/shadow pairing or known hash format; account identity and a feasible recovery strategy\n\n**Recover Linux account passwords from matched records — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5483,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\n**When:** An NT verifier from an appropriate credential source\n\n**Still required:** Correct account/domain and actual NT hash; recovery mode or an accepting NTLM service with required destination rights\n\n**Recover or reuse an NT password hash — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5790,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover a password from a captured NTLM response\n\n**When:** A complete challenge-response record\n\n**Still required:** Correct challenge/response formatting and feasible candidates; acquisition method must fit the allowed context\n\n**Recover a password from a captured NTLM response — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-classify:next-8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6097,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover a password from cached domain logon verifiers\n\n**When:** A DCC2/MSCache record from matched SECURITY/SYSTEM material\n\n**Still required:** Correct username/salt/iteration context and feasible offline candidates\n\n**Recover a password from cached domain logon verifiers — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 6704,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\nA password tied to a plausible user and service",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 6664,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD'\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 6644,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAccepted authentication proves one service/account pairing; it does not establish shares, administration, RDP or WinRM.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 6890,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nQualify local/domain/application identity explicitly, test a compatible reachable service and record the accepted identity. Then test the specific share/logon/execution right; successful authentication is not administrative authorization.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 6904,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD'\nssh -p PORT USER@TARGET\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 6594,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe intended service operation succeeds under the recorded identity: use that access and re-enumerate.\n\n**Verify:** Record exact identity, service and tested read/write/session effect; classify authentication and authorization separately.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#credential-use|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 6935,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe secret is valid only for the application and not the proposed OS account: reject that reuse pairing.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7156,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA generic logon failure may hide account/domain/state mismatch; classify it before repeating attempts.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6594,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -o PreferredAuthentications=password -p PORT USER@TARGET\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD' --shares\nevil-winrm -i TARGET -u USER -p 'PASSWORD'\nxfreerdp /v:TARGET /u:'DOMAIN\\USER' /p:'PASSWORD' /cert:ignore\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#credential-use|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6984,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7291,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:credential-use:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7622,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access\n\n**When:** An SSH service and a known password, private key or agent context\n\n**Still required:** Compatible authentication method, correct user, accepted key policy and the requested shell/subsystem permission\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 8229,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\nA supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 8189,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhashcat --example-hashes\njohn --list=formats\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 8169,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA verified format and feasible candidate model enable offline recovery; a hash-shaped string alone does not.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 8415,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck complete salt/context, conversion correctness, tool backend and whether all required factors are present.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8119,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe verifier and candidate space are valid: use the selected offline strategy and verify recovered credentials.\n\n**Verify:** Use the tool's show/result output and then validate the recovered credential in its correct context.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#offline-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8460,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe artifact is a non-crackable token or unsupported format under this workflow: reject that mode.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8681,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nParsing errors or an incomplete source require input repair; no recovery only exhausts the tested candidates.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8119,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nhashcat -b -m MODE\npython3 -c \"print((CHARSET_SIZE ** LENGTH) / GUESSES_PER_SECOND)\"\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#offline-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8461,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8768,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect and recover SSH private-key access\n\n**When:** A private key from a file read, share, repository or home directory\n\n**Still required:** Correct key format, passphrase if encrypted, matching server account/key authorization and accepted algorithm/policy\n\n**Inspect and recover SSH private-key access — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:offline-recovery:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9075,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery\n\n**When:** A user-owned SPN and a useful service-account relationship\n\n**Still required:** A valid domain authentication/TGT context, reachable KDC, target SPN and a feasible password/encryption candidate strategy\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 9682,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover a protected KeePass database password\n\nA readable KeePass database and possible associated key file",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 9642,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nfile FILE\nkeepass2john FILE > keepass.hash\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 9622,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA supported database gives a recovery target, but a referenced key file indicates a separate factor.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 9868,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm vault version, required key/account factors and a feasible password search.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9572,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nAll required factors are available and the recovered password opens the vault: inspect its typed credentials.\n\n**Verify:** Open the database with all factors and distinguish vault credentials from target account credentials.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#keepass-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9913,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nAn unavailable mandatory key factor prevents this password-only route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10110,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA converter result alone does not identify every required factor; inspect relevant vault configuration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9572,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nkeepass2john vault.kdbx > keepass.hash\njohn --wordlist=wordlist.txt keepass.hash\njohn --show keepass.hash\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#keepass-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9938,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n**Classify the artifact and its identity context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10269,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:keepass-recovery:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10576,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n[[tracks/03 Web.canvas|Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts → 03 Web]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 11207,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Inspect and recover SSH private-key access\n\nA private key from a file read, share, repository or home directory",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 11167,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nfile KEY\nssh-keygen -y -f KEY\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 11147,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe artifact is a private key protected by a local passphrase; this is separate from the SSH account password.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 11393,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nDetermine the protecting passphrase, associated remote user, accepted algorithm and server key authorization.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 11431,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nchmod 600 KEY\nssh-keygen -y -f KEY\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11097,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe key parses and the correct server account accepts it: use its permitted shell/subsystem/forwarding capability.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the key parses and an SSH authentication/session succeeds under the correct target identity.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#ssh-key|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11438,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe artifact contains only a public key: reject private-key authentication with that file.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11659,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA decrypted key rejected by the server leaves username/authorization/policy unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11097,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh2john id_rsa > ssh.hash\njohn --wordlist=wordlist.txt ssh.hash\njohn --show ssh.hash\nchmod 600 id_rsa\nssh-keygen -y -f id_rsa > derived.pub\nssh -vv -i id_rsa -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -p PORT USER@TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#ssh-key|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11535,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access\n\n**When:** An SSH service and a known password, private key or agent context\n\n**Still required:** Compatible authentication method, correct user, accepted key policy and the requested shell/subsystem permission\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11842,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener\n\n**When:** SSH reaches a server that can access the needed internal service\n\n**Still required:** Accepted SSH identity and forwarding policy; local listener availability and SSH-server-to-destination route\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-key:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12149,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 12756,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover Linux account passwords from matched records\n\nReadable password verifiers and account metadata",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 12716,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nfile passwd.txt shadow.txt\nhead -n 3 passwd.txt\nhead -n 3 shadow.txt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 12696,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe matching account name and verifier prefix identify an offline password-recovery candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 12942,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm snapshots, hash format and account state; a locked field or absent salt is not a normal usable verifier.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13004,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nunshadow passwd.txt shadow.txt > linux.hashes\njohn --wordlist=WORDLIST linux.hashes\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12646,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA complete supported verifier and feasible candidate space exist: recover, then validate the matching account.\n\n**Verify:** Tie the recovered password to the correct user and validate an allowed login/sudo transition.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#linux-hashes|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12987,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe password field is locked with no usable verifier: reject recovery from that field.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13208,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nMismatched backups or unknown account scope require source consistency checks.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12646,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nunshadow passwd.copy shadow.copy > linux.hash\njohn --wordlist=wordlist.txt --rules=Jumbo linux.hash\njohn --show linux.hash\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#linux-hashes|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13012,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13319,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use an allowed sudo operation to cross a privilege boundary\n\n**When:** sudo -l grants an operation under a more useful identity\n\n**Still required:** Exact executable/run-as/argument rule permits a useful primitive; password tags, environment and policy do not invalidate it\n\n[[tracks/07 Linux Privilege Escalation.canvas|Use an allowed sudo operation to cross a privilege boundary → 07 Linux Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:linux-hashes:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13626,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Linux state and choose an escalation candidate\n\n**When:** A new Linux foothold or an identity/privilege change\n\n**Still required:** A working command channel and accurate effective identity, group, mount and process context\n\n[[tracks/07 Linux Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Linux state and choose an escalation candidate → 07 Linux Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 14233,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\nAn NT verifier from an appropriate credential source",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 14193,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhead -n 3 hashes.txt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 14173,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe source and record fields identify an NT verifier for that local account, not a captured challenge response.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 14419,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify the actual NT field, account scope and an accepting service/client with the required destination right.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 14433,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nhashcat -m 1000 hashes.txt WORDLIST\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -H HASH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14123,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA compatible service accepts the correctly qualified hash identity: use only its verified authorization.\n\n**Verify:** Verify source/type, identity context and the exact permitted service action.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#nt-hash|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14464,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe source produced Net-NTLMv2 or DCC2 instead: reject direct NT-hash reuse.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14661,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unlabeled hexadecimal value remains unknown until the source/account is resolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14123,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nhashcat -a 0 -m 1000 nt.hash wordlist.txt -r /usr/share/hashcat/rules/best64.rule\njohn --format=NT --wordlist=wordlist.txt nt.hash\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#nt-hash|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14465,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14796,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:nt-hash:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15103,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\n**When:** A destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights\n\n**Still required:** SMB/SCM reachability, writable required share, effective service-creation/start rights and an accepted password/hash or supported Kerberos context\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 15758,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover a password from a captured NTLM response\n\nA complete challenge-response record",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 15718,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhead -n 2 responses.txt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15698,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA challenge-bound response supports its appropriate offline verification workflow; it is not the long-term NT hash.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15944,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck complete capture format, account mapping and feasible candidates; acquisition/relay policy is a separate issue.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 15958,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nhashcat -m 5600 responses.txt WORDLIST\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15648,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA complete supported record permits offline recovery and later password validation.\n\n**Verify:** Retain response provenance and recovered account/password mapping; confirm relevant login rights separately.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#netntlm-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15989,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nUsing this response directly as an NT hash is the wrong mechanism: reject that authentication attempt.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16210,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTruncated challenge/blob fields cannot support a valid recovery conclusion.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15648,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nhashcat -a 0 -m 5600 netntlmv2.hash wordlist.txt\njohn --format=netntlmv2 --wordlist=wordlist.txt netntlmv2.hash\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#netntlm-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15990,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16297,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n**Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:netntlm-recovery:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16604,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route\n\n**When:** Domain credentials or a domain-joined foothold\n\n**Still required:** Correct realm/domain and account qualification; reachable DC/services, usable DNS and acceptable clock skew\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 17211,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover a password from cached domain logon verifiers\n\nA DCC2/MSCache record from matched SECURITY/SYSTEM material",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 17171,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhead -n 3 dcc2.txt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 17151,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe DCC2 structure and username-associated derivation identify offline cached-logon material.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 17397,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify iteration/username context, source consistency and current online account state after any recovery.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 17411,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nhashcat -m 2100 dcc2.txt WORDLIST\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17101,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA complete supported record and feasible candidates enable the DCC2 recovery workflow.\n\n**Verify:** Confirm artifact format, account mapping and current password acceptance.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#dcc2-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17442,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nDCC2 is not accepted directly as an NTLM long-term hash: reject that reuse route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17663,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA recovered old password may be stale; validate current account acceptance without assuming extraction failed.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17101,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nhashcat -hh | grep -i 'Domain Cached'\njohn --format=mscash2 --wordlist=wordlist.txt dcc2.hash\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#dcc2-recovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17443,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n**Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17750,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route\n\n**When:** Domain credentials or a domain-joined foothold\n\n**Still required:** Correct realm/domain and account qualification; reachable DC/services, usable DNS and acceptable clock skew\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:dcc2-recovery:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18057,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n**Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 18664,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Classify tickets and use a compatible cache\n\nA ccache/kirbi file or an existing ticket cache",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 18624,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nklist -c FILE\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18604,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThis is service-scoped CIFS material, not a TGT for requesting arbitrary services.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18850,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck lifetime, cache format, exact SPN/name, route and destination object authorization.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18554,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe matching SMB service accepts the ticket and allowed operation: use that scoped capability.\n\n**Verify:** Inspect principal, ticket service, realm and lifetime, then verify the actual service action.\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#ticket-use|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18895,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nA CIFS-only ticket does not enable a WinRM-specific authentication path.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 19092,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unreadable/expired cache or unknown principal requires inspection/conversion rather than guessed reuse.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18554,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nklist\nKRB5CCNAME=TICKET.ccache klist\nimpacket-ticketConverter TICKET.kirbi TICKET.ccache\n```\n\n[[notes/credentials.md#ticket-use|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18920,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19251,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ticket-use:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19582,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "track-title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# 05 Credentials\n\nAll workflows, commands, result interpretations and method connections for this track are on this canvas. Embedded notes contain the complete procedures and variants.\n\n[[START.canvas|Choose another track]]\n\nCross-track results link directly to the receiving track."
    }
  ],
